# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# security assessments — these name the unprotected routes and the ungated
# actions. This repo is public; do not commit them.
ASSESSMENT.md
DATA-ROW-DRAWER.md

# sql — local dumps, backups and scratch queries stay out of the repo.
# The two exceptions below are load-bearing and must remain tracked:
#   db/schema.sql      — scripts/check-schema.mjs reads it, and nothing else in
#                        CI has a database. It is the only place the frozen
#                        column list of public.visible_contacts is visible
#                        offline, so untracking it would silently disable the
#                        one check that catches a column the view lost.
#   db/migrations/*.sql — the record of what has actually been applied, and the
#                        same check reads every migration that defines the view.
#                        If a new migration is ignored here, schema.sql drifts
#                        stale and the check passes against old truth.
*.sql
!db/schema.sql
!db/migrations/*.sql

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
